% Inline, params and debug are three ways of joining one part list, not three
% code paths. The renderer never concatenates a literal into a string.

### name: mode.inline.is-the-default
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
T > 100 AND T < 200
--- expect
((`t` > 100) AND (`t` < 200))
===
### name: mode.params.placeholders-in-order
--- dialect
mariadb
--- mode
params
--- bindings
{"T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
T > 100 AND T < 200
--- expect
((`t` > ?) AND (`t` < ?))
--- params
t"100", t"200"
===
### name: mode.debug.slots-are-visible
--- dialect
mariadb
--- mode
debug
--- bindings
{"T": {"kind": "column", "column": "t", "type": "NUM"}}
--- source
T > 100 AND T < 200
--- expect
((`t` > ~1~) AND (`t` < ~2~))
===
### name: mode.params.a-literal-holding-a-placeholder-stays-a-literal
--- note
The reason a part list exists. Inline, the ? is inside a quoted string; in
params mode the real placeholder is a separate slot and the two never mix.
--- dialect
mariadb
--- mode
params
--- bindings
{"S": {"kind": "column", "column": "s", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- source
S $== "?"
--- expect
(`s` COLLATE utf8mb4_bin = ? COLLATE utf8mb4_bin)
--- params
t"?"
===
### name: mode.params.same-expression-inline
--- dialect
mariadb
--- bindings
{"S": {"kind": "column", "column": "s", "type": "TEXT"}}
--- source
S $== "?"
--- expect
(`s` COLLATE utf8mb4_bin = '?' COLLATE utf8mb4_bin)
===
### name: mode.params.order-follows-the-text-not-the-tree
--- dialect
mariadb
--- mode
params
--- source
COND(TRUE, "a", "b")
--- expect
CASE WHEN ? THEN ? ELSE ? END
--- params
TRUE, t"a", t"b"
